      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5c1d007d3d7a0912aaff65e8|full_name}: Nope. It's entirely possible. It's just a matter of telling unity to stop using the assembly and run your update code in a separate assembly. If you have no idea what I'm talking about, means you don't know about how code in Unity at a very low level.\n\n... though most makers avoid auto-updates because stuff breaks, especially when a release supports/deprecates a major Unity version or majorly changes the codebase (like adding/removing/moving functions). For example, the operating system you're using right now to play the game (AKA. Windows 10).",
